POST /auth/register: authController.

Authentication: Public; no bearer. Tenant header: not required.     

Headers: Content-Type. Path parameters: none. Success status: 201.

Body: raw. Input JSON schema (required fields and supported optional fields):
{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "email": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "email",
      "pattern": "^(?:[A-Za-z0-9_'+\\-]+\\.)*[A-Za-z0-9_'+\\-]*[A-Za-z0-9_+-]@(?:[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9\\-]*\\.)+[A-Za-z]{2,}$"
    },
    "password": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 8,
      "maxLength": 128,
      "allOf": [
        {
          "pattern": "[A-Z]"
        },
        {
          "pattern": "[a-z]"
        },
        {
          "pattern": "[0-9]"
        },
        {
          "pattern": "[^A-Za-z0-9]"
        }
      ]
    },
    "firstName": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1,
      "maxLength": 100
    },
    "lastName": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1,
      "maxLength": 100
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "email",
    "password",
    "firstName",
    "lastName"
  ]
}

Query: none documented by route validation.

Important module business errors: ACCOUNT_INACTIVE, AUTHENTICATION_REQUIRED, EMAIL_ALREADY_EXISTS, INVALID_CREDENTIALS, INVALID_CURRENT_PASSWORD, INVALID_PASSWORD_RESET_TOKEN, INVALID_REFRESH_TOKEN, INVALID_VERIFICATION_TOKEN, PASSWORD_RESET_TOKEN_ALREADY_USED, PASSWORD_RESET_TOKEN_EXPIRED, REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRED, REFRESH_TOKEN_REUSED, USER_NOT_FOUND, VALIDATION_ERROR, VERIFICATION_TOKEN_ALREADY_USED, VERIFICATION_TOKEN_EXPIRED. Shared failures include AUTHENTICATION_REQUIRED/INVALID_ACCESS_TOKEN (protected requests), UNAUTHORIZED/TENANT_NOT_FOUND (tenant context), FORBIDDEN (roles), and VALIDATION_ERROR. Business errors retain {success:false,message,code,data:null}.

Side effects: may modify state; requires allowMutations=true; do not run against existing/production data without explicit intent.. 

Registration creates a global CUSTOMER identity and returns a user without tokens. Verification/reset delivery may use the private development file outbox. Never log secrets. Set authProfile=customer/owner/admin before login/refresh; each profile has separate tokens. Refresh is single-use: serialize requests and replace the rotated pair.

